#. Tag: title
#: playing-music.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid "Music Players"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: playing-music.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are several &kde; music players with somewhat overlapping feature "
"sets, however, each is quite different in style."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: playing-music.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>&noatun;</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: playing-music.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>&noatun;</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: playing-music.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Noatun is the default &kde; music player. It features a highly configurable "
"interface, including several styles of playlist manager, and many plugins to "
"provide different &GUI;s, visualizations, and other features."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: playing-music.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid "&noatun; is part of the kdemultimedia package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: playing-music.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>&juk;</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: playing-music.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>&juk;</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: playing-music.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&juk; is a media manager, playlist manager, and metadata tagger. It is a "
"highly efficient way to manage all your music files, make and maintain "
"playlists, and maintain the metadata tags in your music."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: playing-music.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is equally useful as your primary music player, or managing playlists and "
"files for use in another application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: playing-music.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "&juk; is part of the kdemultimedia package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: playing-music.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>&kaboodle;</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: playing-music.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>&kaboodle;</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: playing-music.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kaboodle; is a one shot player. That means, it will run, play a file, and "
"stop. &kaboodle; is useful for instance if you want to quickly listen to a "
"single file without interupting your current playlist from another media "
"player."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: playing-music.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kaboodle; is part of the kdemultimedia package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: application
#: playing-music.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "amaroK"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: playing-music.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<application>amaroK</application> is a popular third party application. You "
"should be able to find packages from your normal distribution source."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: playing-music.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most of the &kde; based movie players such as <application>Kaffeine</"
"application> and <application>kmplayer</application> also make useful music "
"players."
msgstr ""

